
;==========================================================================
;                       (UPH) UNIVERSAL PROGRAM HEADER                           
;==========================================================================
;                              Copy—&—Paste 
;==========================================================================
;                                   —
;==========================================================================
;   OBJECTIVE: IMPLEMENT THE EXAMPLE IN FIGURE [4.7]
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------
;==========================================================================
;                          HIGH-LEVEL BREAKDOWN    
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------
; 1. **Load first operand (multiplicand)**  
;   - Load the value at memory location `x3007` (which is `5`) into register `R1`.

; 2. **Load second operand (multiplier)**  
;   - Load the value at memory location `x3008` (which is `4`) into register `R2`.

; 3. **Initialize result register**  
;   - Set register `R3` to `0`. This will hold the final product.

; 4. **Start loop: add R1 to R3**  
;   - Add the value in `R1` to `R3`. This simulates one multiplication step.

; 5. **Decrement R2**  
;   - Subtract `1` from `R2`. This tracks how many additions remain.

; 6. **Check loop condition**  
;   - If `R2` is not zero, branch back to step 4 and repeat.

; 7. **End loop and halt**  
;   - Once `R2` reaches zero, the loop exits and the program halts.

; 8. **Final result**  
;   - Register `R3` now contains the product of `5 × 4 = 20`.
;==========================================================================
;                          REGISTER CONVENTION
;==========================================================================
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------
; R0    : Unused temporary register                         
; EOP   : 0
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------
; R1    : Multiplicand (value from x3007)                  
; EOP   : 5
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------
; R2    : Multiplier (value from x3008), decremented each loop
; EOP   : 4
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------
; R3    : Accumulator for result (R1 × R2)                 
; EOP   : 20
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------
; R4    : Unused                                            
; EOP   : 0
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------
; R5    : Unused                                            
; EOP   : 0
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------
; R6    : Unused                                            
; EOP   : 0
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------
; R7    : Unused                                            
; EOP   : 0
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------
;==========================================================================

0011000000000000        ;   .ORIG x3000
0010 001 000000110      ;   R1 <- M[x3007]
0010 010 000000110      ;   R2 <- M[x3008]
0101011000000000        ;   R3 <- 0
0001011011000001        ;   R3 <- R3 + R1
0001010010111111        ;   R2 <- R2 - 1
0000001 1 1111 1101     ;   BRp x3003
1111000000100101        ;   HALT
0000000000000101        ;   Data: 5
0000000000000100        ;   Data: 4

